  "verbalization": "Miyabenol A is shown to have a target relationship with U251 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link being to 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is also targeted by WS-5995 B. This suggests that Miyabenol A may act through a common mechanism involving the proteasome system, potentially modulating protein degradation processes in U251 cells. The second pathway links Miyabenol A to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by a complex compound with a known structure, further supporting a role in proteasome-related functions. The final_score values indicate a moderate level of confidence in these relationships, suggesting that Miyabenol A may exert its effects through a proteasome-dependent mechanism, possibly influencing cellular processes in U251. The evidence supports a mechanistic connection between Miyabenol A and U251, though the exact molecular pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
